  "content": {
    "id": "p81-q50-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Given the cubic function $f(x)$ has a double zero at $x=-1$, a single zero at $x=2$ and the graph of $y=f(x)$ has a $y$-intercept of $4$, find $f(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p81-q50-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "f(x)=-2(x+1)^2(x-2)",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p81-q50-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "f(0)=4",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " in ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "f(x)=k(x+1)^2(x-2)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " to obtain ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "-2k=4",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", so ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "k=-2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The double zero gives the factor $(x+1)^2$, and the single zero gives the factor $(x-2)$. The $y$-intercept gives $f(0)=4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nf(x) &= k(x+1)^2(x-2) \\\\\n4 &= k(0+1)^2(0-2) \\\\\nk &= -2 \\\\\nf(x) &= -2(x+1)^2(x-2).\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
